+# Scheduled posts are hidden at read time
+
+## Context
+
+Authors want to write a post now and have it go live later. Until then the
+post must exist only for its author; afterwards it must be public without
+anyone pressing a button and without anything having to run at that moment.
+
+## Decision
+
+`posts.published_at` is a nullable ISO 8601 timestamp stored as text, like
+`created_at`. `NULL` or a time in the past means public; a later time means
+scheduled. There is no status column and no job that publishes posts: every
+read compares `published_at` against the clock.
+
+The rule lives in `app/Models/Post.ts` and nowhere else:
+
+- `Post.visibleTo(viewerId)` is the rule in SQL, for anything that lists
+  posts (the posts list, search, the home page).
+- `Post.isScheduled(post)` is the rule for one record. `PostPolicy.view` and
+  `PostResource` use it.
+- `Post.scheduled()` is its inverse, for the `posts:scheduled` report.
+
+Three choices that are easy to undo by accident:
+
+1. **A hidden post answers 404, not 403.** `PostController` checks
+   `PostPolicy.view` before `authorize()` in every action that loads one
+   post, including edit, update and delete, and throws the same
+   `ModelNotFoundException` a missing id does. A 403 would confirm that the
+   post exists.
+2. **`published_at` is always written as `Date#toISOString()`.** The SQL
+   comparison is on text, which orders as time only while every value has
+   that one shape. The validator requires an offset on `publishAt` and the
+   controller normalizes it to UTC before saving.
+3. **A request without `publishAt` clears the date.** Create and edit send
+   the whole post, so an absent field means "publish now" on both.
+
+The home page passes `null` to `Post.visibleTo()`: it shows public posts
+only, even to the author of a scheduled one.
+
+`bin/console.ts` sends what the framework logs while booting to stderr, so
+that a command's stdout holds only what the command printed.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Going live costs nothing and cannot be missed by a stopped worker. In
+  return, nothing happens at the publish time, so anything that must
+  (notifying subscribers, clearing a cache) needs a scheduler of its own.
+- Any new query that reads posts for display must start from
+  `Post.visibleTo()`. `Post.newQuery()` and `Post.find()` see every post.
+- A `published_at` written by hand in another shape (no milliseconds, a
+  non-UTC offset) is compared as text and can be off by up to the offset
+  near the publish time. `Post.isScheduled` parses the value instead and
+  treats one it cannot read as scheduled.
+- The author sees their own scheduled posts in search results too.
diff --git a/resources/js/components/PublishAtField.tsx b/resources/js/components/PublishAtField.tsx
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d1ad2db
--- /dev/null
+++ b/resources/js/components/PublishAtField.tsx
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+import { useEffect, useState } from 'react'
+
+interface Props {
+  // What the server takes: an ISO 8601 UTC timestamp, or null to publish now.
+  value: string | null
+  onChange: (value: string | null) => void
+  error?: string
+  className?: string
+}
+
+// `datetime-local` speaks the viewer's wall-clock time with no zone attached.
+function toLocalInput(iso: string): string {
+  const date = new Date(iso)
+  if (Number.isNaN(date.getTime())) {
+    return ''
+  }
+  const pad = (part: number) => String(part).padStart(2, '0')
+  return `${date.getFullYear()}-${pad(date.getMonth() + 1)}-${pad(date.getDate())}T${pad(date.getHours())}:${pad(date.getMinutes())}`
+}
+
+function fromLocalInput(local: string): string | null {
+  const date = new Date(local)
+  return local === '' || Number.isNaN(date.getTime()) ? null : date.toISOString()
+}
+
+export default function PublishAtField({ value, onChange, error, className }: Props) {
+  const [local, setLocal] = useState('')
+
+  // Filled in after mount, not during render: the server renders in its own
+  // time zone, and a value that differs from the browser's breaks hydration.
+  useEffect(() => {
+    setLocal(value ? toLocalInput(value) : '')
+    // Only the value the form opened with; later ones come from this input.
+  }, [])
+
+  return (
+    <div>
+      <label htmlFor="publishAt" className="block text-sm font-bold text-g-heading">
+        Publish at
+      </label>
+      <input
+        id="publishAt"
+        type="datetime-local"
+        value={local}
+        onChange={(event) => {
+          setLocal(event.target.value)
+          onChange(fromLocalInput(event.target.value))
+        }}
+        className={className}
+      />
+      <p className="mt-1 text-sm text-g-muted">
+        In your local time. Leave empty to publish as soon as you save; until a later time only you can see the post.
+      </p>
+      {error ? <p className="mt-1 text-sm text-g-danger">{error}</p> : null}
+    </div>
+  )
+}
